 procurement by contracting with sources who \nadequately compen","path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/texts/cd-job-fr-originals-13658-acaaad8df7.txt","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"69fb2c44ee7b49a60bdb1819d71db365dcfd6cac5f63cb8d48704d76f8487c1c","source":{"line":9011,"path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"6c98d677caf1bd03cebd488d963e9d9b084cf7a9972f9980d1fd26e429bf798a"}},{"first_1500_characters":"{\"member\": \"usc02.xml\", \"note_id\": \"iddcb8117d-3a6e-11f1-a0f3-db3efcbbb4ee\", \"citation\": \"2 U.S.C. 685 note\", \"heading\": \"Ex. Ord. No. 11845. Delegation of Certain Reporting Functions to Director of Office of Management and Budget\", \"subjects\": [\"11845\"], \"status_line\": \"Ex. Ord. No. 11845, Mar. 24, 1975, 40 F.R. 13299, as amended by Ex. Ord. No. 12608, Sept. 9, 1987, 52 F.R. 34617, provided:\", \"t","path":"jobs/current-law/output/USC_EO_NOTES.jsonl","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"ac1e287b6b606b8adc5c1975f662aae2d31989c1d072e32c89dbc38f6efe8016","source":{"line":3,"path":"jobs/current-law/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"db3e7966c86bf015e11638031156112944d0b0fb96a2d7dd0e00324b4eada8a2"}},{"first_1500_characters":"Instrument: EO:13658\nSource: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2014-02-20/pdf/2014-03805.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: acaaad8df7b7f4556a1150c81d0f3c8d8097ffc8d3264adefc32ca814c27ed0c\nLocation: 79 FR 9851, PDF pages 1-4 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the s","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_13658.txt","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"5b31769d2d01a61e1d9b0cb94d57b0b16eee9f31496a77ca0f30ed4b5ebf63b1","source":{"line":2157,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"f5676cd0e8f6421feeab85f7e1390fb4faa757c2db480a977288b51ccbb7d652"}},{"first_1500_characters":"§ 10.1 Purpose and scope.\n(a) Purpose. This part contains the Department of Labor's rules relating to the administration of Executive Order 13658 (Executive Order or the Order), “Establishing a Minimum Wage for Contractors,” and implements the enforcement provisions of the Executive Order. The Executive Order assigns responsibility for investigating potential violations of and obtaining compliance","path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/texts/cfr-t29-10.1.txt","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"c80867bd0621a0af404b94d5aa437e8ff65bfd6a18c7684577ccd2d1446ef5cd","source":{"line":109,"path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"e8b2c2fbd34c5d868d6a3110f89ffc79fc3322763841ba0de532b36bc13ed1c5"}},{"first_1500_characters":"§ 10.11 Contracting agency requirements.\n(a) Contract clause. The contracting agency shall include the Executive Order minimum wage contract clause set forth in appendix A of this part in all covered contracts and solicitations for such contracts, as described in § 10.3, except for procurement contracts subject to the FAR. The required contract clause directs, as a condition of payment, that all w","path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/texts/cfr-t29-10.11.txt","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"cce96e48cd2d1cbe0d53e38a42715e83a2c1352608c2f7a119a4c0b0c8cc17db","source":{"line":110,"path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"d0905cb5ec931622efb14118d8c1c472501f8ce41d78a8d6d469da542addb202"}},{"first_1500_characters":"§ 10.5 Minimum wage for Federal contractors and subcontractors.\n(a) General. Pursuant to Executive Order 13658, the minimum hourly wage rate required to be paid to workers performing on or in connection with covered contracts with the Federal Government is at least:\n(1) $10.10 per hour beginning January 1, 2015; and\n(2) Beginning January 1, 2016, and annually thereafter, an amount determined by th","path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/texts/cfr-t29-10.5.txt","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"44c9b8b8396c5d649ea4723224572c0a5af482808eaa38cff71cf29b24f7c2b7","source":{"line":111,"path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"567de022b012fa6faca4080af4f9abdb906a7d7ec98478a0356b0d6d63f34754"}},{"first_1500_characters":"§ 10.52 Debarment proceedings.\n(a) Whenever any contractor is found by the Secretary of Labor to have disregarded its obligations to workers or subcontractors under Executive Order 13658 or this part, such contractor and its responsible officers, and any firm, corporation, partnership, or association in which such contractor or responsible officers have an interest, shall be ineligible for a perio","path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/texts/cfr-t29-10.52.txt","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"cffe535db8f16825f035e2ba9e77b5849bd41d82754cb42105b70ac494f94553","source":{"line":112,"path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"a262a8616c25e9d953085873034b07630a02938f5163fe2cde4d7c0e50faa2d3"}},{"first_1500_characters":"§ 23.20 Definitions.\nFor purposes of this part:\nAdministrative Review Board (ARB or Board) means the Administrative Review Board, U.S. Department of Labor.\nAdministrator means the Administrator of the Wage and Hour Division and includes any official of the Wage and Hour Division authorized to perform any of the functions of the Administrator under this part.\nAgency head means the Secretary, Attorn","path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/texts/cfr-t29-23.20.txt","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"e75479655c0fda95a55b1faaee05fa86c211ad02fd9f98d2fd8a12e0424a4f34","source":{"line":121,"path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"3338c147fd6071c6c8bad612cf70564faf4154dcc08b17eb1e9e5d443e4b202c"}},{"first_1500_characters":"PART 10—ESTABLISHING A MINIMUM WAGE FOR CONTRACTORS\nAuthority:5 U.S.C. 301; section 4, E.O. 13658, 79 FR 9851, 3 CFR, 2014 Comp., p. 219; section 4, E.O. 14026, 86 FR 22835; Secretary of Labor's Order No. 01-2014, 79 FR 77527.\nSource:79 FR 60721, Oct. 7, 2014, unless otherwise noted.\nSubpart A—General\n§ 10.1 Purpose and scope.\n(a) Purpose. This part contains the Department of Labor's rules relatin","path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/texts/cfr-t29-part10.txt","preview_truncated_for_budget":true,"sha256":"454241a4105334dbc156f912c55d58f6b8b1fe158d2e8caca41d45eb594a083b","source":{"line":122,"path":"jobs/theophilus-sources/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"b251ebc015e107e15c9f56ecbefb61628cd6f0764eb68f3676e1fe3adc60bb8e"}}]}
